{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/956089-perchance-to-dream-the-astral-chronicle-collaborative","id":956089,"title":"Perchance to Dream: The Astral Chronicle [Collaborative]","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-08-22T19:43:25-07:00","id":956089,"title":"Perchance to Dream: The Astral Chronicle [Collaborative]","content":"So I've been sitting on the rough skeleton of this for months, resulting from an internal struggle to make the Beast material something I'd be excited to work with instead of just joining the tired chorus of moaning about it. The thing I seized onto (with the help of <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar70_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"70\" data-vbnamecard=\"70\">MachineIV</a> and their awesome Merrick Institute) was how the Astral has grown to be a surprisingly busy corner of the Chronicles of Darkness cosmology, and how telling a story about the people and not-people that visit it might be fun. So I'm not sure where this thread is supposed to go, other than a spot to share an idea I've been working on while I've waited for my insomnia meds to work over the last few weeks. If anyone wants to pitch in with related ideas (or just lambast it for being terrible), fire away.<br /> <br /> Here's the pitch:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In the distant center of the Pacific Ocean, opposing currents carry the collective refuse of Asia and North America on a grand trash pilgrimage to a swirling gyre the size of Texas composed of waste, known to scientists as the Great Pacific Garbage Patch. In many ways, the shared subconscious of the human race (and it's closest cousins, who live in the shadows) is much like a great sea, with esoteric tides that sweep away discarded concepts when they cease to be relevant. Within this sea of thoughts, there exists a thing roughly analogous to the Great Pacific Garbage Patch, an infinite plastic beach made up of dead gods, childhood fears, forgotten memories, and abandoned dreams, the mental detritus of an entire species and the world it lives on. Travelers along the roads of thought sometimes find themselves deposited in this nameless place, and it is they who we tell our story about.<br /> <br /> One is a little girl, whose nightmares devoured her heart and took up residence in the bloody hollow left behind. One is a lost man, stolen away to Somewhere Else and returned as a patchwork of stolen dreams. One is a scholar who consumes Mysteries of the mind and finds his feeding grows his Obsession, rather than sates it. One is an unwilling traveler who escaped her broken body at the behest of another, and finds she can no longer go home. One has long ago forgotten what they once were, having turned their soul inside out in order to live forever as a dead thing. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-22T20:04:18-07:00","id":956097,"title":"","content":"I like this. I had an idea for a Ghost oriented one that I'm almost read to post (but I digress).<br /> <br /> What direction are you planning on taking this in? Exploration of the Astral itself? How different things interact with the Astral?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-22T20:10:22-07:00","id":956103,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/956089-perchance-to-dream-the-astral-chronicle-collaborative?p=956097#post956097\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like this. I had an idea for a Ghost oriented one that I'm almost read to post (but I digress).<br /> <br /> What direction are you planning on taking this in? Exploration of the Astral itself? How different things interact with the Astral?</div> </div> </div> </div>Crossover focused on the Astral and and excuse to do a CofD chronicle that's entirely left the material world behind, while still being mysterious and horrifying.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-23T06:28:15-07:00","id":956287,"title":"","content":"Speaking of Beast, back in 2014 when it was first being announced as the gameline of 2015 and we were only given the clue that it would be subversive, I got an idea. Inspired by the <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=58TYbxrUIjc\" target=\"_blank\">Deep Sleep flash game series</a>, I thought of ordinary people who somehow were caught into a deep dreamspace where it became difficult for them to wake up from. When they did wake back up, there was a chance they'd enter again the next time they slept, which became more and more likely as they gained a greater connection to the dreamspace (the consequence of raising their power stat). What's worse, supernaturals often ended up there, too. Several were eventually consumed by the dreamspace and melded together to become unique, horrific monstrosities unlike anything else.<br /> <br /> What's funny is that I thought a game like this wasn't likely at all, and that the alien gameline idea others had proposed was far more likely. But it turns out my idea was far closer to what Beast is than the alien idea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2992-crapcarp","name":"crapcarp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-23T07:38:25-07:00","id":956310,"title":"","content":"Hmm. I was thinking up a group that leveraged their Goetia to their advantage. Purely Oneiros (personal mind/soul space) level. They'd basically be exploiting the fact that the Ephemerals are a part of them to leverage things like Influence being used to help whatever goal or drive the Goetia represents. Maxed out in incarnating the Goetic drive (Claim) for power. Of course, that somewhat relies on my personal houseruling which doesn't prevent Goetia from getting Manifestations &quot;naturally&quot; (like every other Ephemeral). Still, the ability to add Manifestations to one's personal Goetia is a small step.<br /> <br /> I'd imagine such a group would be interested in the greater Astral as well (Temenos, Skein, or Dream).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-24T18:34:27-07:00","id":957310,"title":"","content":"I'm somewhat reminded of this trailer.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=YKejRIdDeN0\" data-code=\"YKejRIdDeN0\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/YKejRIdDeN0/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-24T19:46:33-07:00","id":957343,"title":"","content":"(Guess this will be my first post on the forums)<br /> <br /> Since being introduced to the World/Chronicles of Darkness via Changeling I have been deeply interested in the means to explore and utilize the surreal landscape of dreams for storytelling. I've been running a crossover game for close to a year now with an emphasis on dreaming as built into some fan splats.<br /> <br /> But for starters, I've been curious about the means of comparing 'dreaming' mechanics from the official game lines.<br /> <br /> <b>Changelings</b> are able to travel, observe and influence dreams as they connect to the Hedge, unless they have certain kinds of contracts. Dreams are said to have an Intensity rating, at least in 1E. A number of successes were needed to reach a dream under default abilities. The Intensity would have to be scoured or surpasses to make lasting changes to the dream. Changelings had the means of using their attributes and skills within dreams, often Empathy or Occult was used along with Wyrd in the dice pool.<br /> <br /> I am not as familiar with <b>Mage</b> rules for dreaming, although I'm correct in thinking these abilities sit under the Mind Arcana for Mages? It also appears Mage was the first and main classifier of the areas of the Astral &quot;Dreaming.&quot; The Oneiros, the dreams, thoughts &amp; memories of an individual; the Temenos, the collected dreams of humanity; and the Anima Mundi, the dream-soul of the universe.<br /> <br /> In <b>Beast</b> it was introduced that the Lairs for each Beast, where the Soul resides, are within the darker parts of the Primordial Dream suspended between the Temenos and Anima Mundi. When the Soul ravages others with the Beast's nightmares it can crash into the Oneiros of others, inflicting fear and often gestating Heroes. When outlining the Dream Form of both Beasts and mortals, the mechanics are for converting the Attributes into their Power, Finesse and Resistance either based on Mental attributes (mortals and most others) or the best attribute in each category for Beasts. Dream health is derived from Resolve and Supernatural Advantage.<br /> <br /> Last to my knowledge in 1E <b>Promethean</b> had the Dream Sharing Bestowment, which allowed the Created to enter the dreams of others. Otherwise they did not normally dream unless they were granted a vision by the Quashmallim. Did this Bestowment return in 2E or were the mechanics expanded? And wasn't there a 'Lineage' where a Promethean could be created from a pervasive meme believed in from enough people?<br /> <br /> What other Dreaming mechanics exist in other venues?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12284-metablender","name":"-metablender","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12284_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-24T21:53:26-07:00","id":957399,"title":"","content":"The idea of a maelstrom in the Temenos made up of dead dreams and lost ideas has great potential. A way to play out all of those 'Lost World' stories.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T08:27:58-07:00","id":957630,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>2ptTakrill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/956089-perchance-to-dream-the-astral-chronicle-collaborative?p=957399#post957399\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The idea of a maelstrom in the Temenos made up of dead dreams and lost ideas has great potential. A way to play out all of those 'Lost World' stories.</div> </div> </div> </div>I thought dead dreams and lost ideas fell into the Underworld. The Grave Dream, I think it was called.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T19:01:19-07:00","id":957991,"title":"","content":"I don't know about the Underworld but the Astral book talks about how anything once part of the Temenos, such as ancient gods, still exist within it even after the modern world has forgotten them. They are weaker than current beliefs but still hiding within the cracks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}